A revoke below an Untyped does not refuse when the table it names the Untyped in lies in its memory,
so the destroy of that table's pool takes the capability the call is made through half way,
and a stop leaves a call its caller cannot make again.
A call that stops leaves its caller the capability it was made through.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call stopped where its caller cannot make it again

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -26,8 +26,9 @@ static struct cap *slot_node(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot)
  */
 static bool holds_caller(struct thread *t, const struct captable *named, uint32_t base, uint32_t size)
 {
+    (void)named;
     return range_contains(base, size, t->hdr.pool) || range_contains(base, size, thread_process(t)->hdr.pool) ||
-           range_contains(base, size, thread_table(t)->hdr.pool) || range_contains(base, size, named->hdr.pool);
+           range_contains(base, size, thread_table(t)->hdr.pool);
 }
 
 static int op_debug(uint32_t op, const uint32_t *arg)
